      "writtenOn": "2022-06-01T18:19:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Zephyr convention is to define shared names in the dt-bindings file, and then have the header file include the bindings file.\n\nProbably best to follow what was done for the USB muxes.  If compiling Zephyr, use the dt-bindings file as the source of truth. This allows the legacy EC to have a single source of flags, and Zephyr EC to have it\u0027s own single source.\n\nhttp://cs/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/include/usb_mux.h?rcl\u003d086009f55adcee29e4d3d8d8d0379d13a99ce946\u0026l\u003d21",
